afers and chips, and other electronic devices. Applied Materials, Inc. was incorporated in 1967 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.","ceo":"Mr. Gary E. Dickerson","headquarters":"Santa Clara, CA","employees":35500,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.appliedmaterials.com","price":435.44,"changePercent":6.07087,"marketCap":345569492992,"peRatio":44.660515,"forwardPE":30.25101,"psRatio":12.248157,"pbRatio":15.912297,"evToEbitda":38.727,"dividendYield":0.49,"beta":1.654,"high52Week":438.04,"low52Week":153.47,"avgVolume":6751637},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":28213.999616,"grossProfit":13747.00032,"operatingIncome":7111.1999488,"netIncome":7839.000064,"ebitda":8888.999936,"totalAssets":56427.999232,"totalDebt":7190.000128,"cashAndEquivalents":8511.000064,"sharesOutstanding":793.609867,"eps":9.75,"dividendsPerShare":2.12,"capex":1410.6999808000005,"operatingCashFlow":8718.999552}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Technology","summary":"Applied Materials, Inc. is well positioned to capture market share in Semiconductor Equipment & Materials.","priceTarget":522.528,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"APP":{"info":{"ticker":"APP","name":"Applovin Corporation","sector":"Communication Services","industry":"Advertising Agencies","description":"AppLovin Corporation provides end-to-end artificial intelligence-powered advertising solutions for businesses in the United States and internationally. It operates through two segments, Advertising and Apps. The company offers Axon Ads Manager, a suite of marketing solutions that enables developers to automate, optimize, and manage marketing efforts; MAX, an in-app bidding technology that optimizes the value of a publisher's advertising inventory by running a real-time competitive auction; Adjust, a measurement and analytics marketing platform; and Wurl, a connected TV platform, which distributes streaming video for content companies, provides advertising and publishing solutions. It serves individuals, small and independent businesses, enterprises, advertisers and advertising networks, mobile app publishers, and indie studio developers. The company was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in Palo Alto, California.","ceo":"Mr. Adam Arash Foroughi","headquarters":"Palo Alto, CA","employees":876,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.applovin.com","price":468.55,"changePercent":-6.07774,"marketCap":157404463104,"peRatio":40.81446,"forwardPE":21.517193,"psRatio":25.535294,"pbRatio":66.66904,"evToEbitda":32.532,"dividendYield":0,"beta":2.366,"high52Week":745.61,"low52Week":320.0,"avgVolume":5316381},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":6164.192256,"grossProfit":5447.099904,"operatingIncome":3897.6446464,"netIncome":3914.972928,"ebitda":4872.055808,"totalAssets":12328.384512,"totalDebt":3849.840128,"cashAndEquivalents":2758.671104,"sharesOutstanding":305.732,"eps":11.48,"dividendsPerShare":0,"capex":308.2096128,"operatingCashFlow":4439.2832}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Communication Services","summary":"Applovin Corporation is well positioned to capture market share in Advertising Agencies.","priceTarget":562.26,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"ARM":{"info":{"ticker":"ARM","name":"Arm Holdings plc","sector":"Technology","industry":"Semiconductors","description":"Arm Holdings plc architects, develops, and licenses central processing unit products and related technologies for semiconductor companies and original equipment manufacturers. The company is involved in the licensing, marketing, research, and development of microprocessors, systems intellectual property (IPs), graphics processing units, physical IP and associated systems IPs, software, tools, and other related services. It also offers arm central processing units, accelerators, system IP products, and compute platform products, as well as development tools and software. The company's products are used in various markets, such as automotive, computing infrastructure, consumer technologies, and Internet of things. It operates in the United States, the People's Republic of China, Taiwan, the Republic of Korea, and internationally. The company was founded in 1990 and is headquartered in Cambridge, the United Kingdom. Arm Holdings plc operates as a subsidiary of SoftBank Group Corp.","ceo":"Mr. Rene Anthony Andrada  Haas","headquarters":"Cambridge, N/A","employees":9584,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.arm.com","price":213.27,"changePercent":-0.0285891,"marketCap":226918989824,"peRatio":250.90588,"forwardPE":71.018745,"psRatio":48.580387,"pbRatio":29.04399,"evToEbitda":206.056,"dividendYield":0,"beta":3.406,"high52Week":239.5,"low52Week":100.02,"avgVolume":7679991},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":4671.000064,"grossProfit":4553.999872,"operatingIncome":867.0400512,"netIncome":801.0,"ebitda":1083.800064,"totalAssets":9342.000128,"totalDebt":432.0,"cashAndEquivalents":3600.999936,"sharesOutstanding":1063.998569,"eps":0.85,"dividendsPerShare":0,"capex":233.5500032,"operatingCashFlow":1522.0}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Technology","summary":"Arm Holdings plc is well positioned to capture market share in Semiconductors.","priceTarget":255.924,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"ASML":{"info":{"ticker":"ASML","name":"ASML Holding N.V. - New York Re","sector":"Technology","industry":"Semiconductor Equipment & Materials","description":"ASML Holding N.V. provides lithography solutions for the development, production, marketing, sales, upgrading, and servicing of advanced semiconductor equipment systems. The company offers lithography, metrology, and inspection systems. It also provides extreme ultraviolet lithography systems; and deep ultraviolet lithography systems comprising immersion and dry lithography systems solutions to manufacture various range of semiconductor nodes and technologies. In addition, the company offers metrology and inspection systems, including YieldStar optical metrology systems, a diffraction-based wafer metrology platform to assess the quality of patterns on the wafers; and HMI electron beam solutions to locate and analyze individual chip defects. Further, it provides computational lithography solutions, and lithography systems and control software solutions; and refurbishes and upgrades lithography systems, as well as offers customer support and related services. Additionally, the company offers hardware, software, and services to chipmakers to produce the patterns of integrated circuits. It operates in Japan, South Korea, Singapore, Taiwan, China, rest of Asia, the Netherlands, rest of Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and the United States. The company was formerly known as ASM Lithography Holding N.V. and changed its name to ASML Holding N.V. in 2001. ASML Holding N.V. was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Veldhoven, the Netherlands.","ceo":"Mr. Christophe D. Fouquet","headquarters":"Veldhoven, N/A","employees":43882,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.asml.com","price":1592.02,"changePercent":4.97297,"marketCap":613592662016,"peRatio":52.35186,"forwardPE":33.05493,"psRatio":18.211441,"pbRatio":1395.6051,"evToEbitda":47.849,"dividendYield":0.55,"beta":1.373,"high52Week":1595.31,"low52Week":683.48,"avgVolume":1677121},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":33692.700672,"grossProfit":17723.29984,"operatingIncome":10163.5203072,"netIncome":10011.10016,"ebitda":