 managing data in one central location, accelerate design processes, and streamline internal/external collaboration. The company offers Flow Production Tracking, a cloud-based production management software; Maya software that offers 3D modeling, animation, effects, rendering, and compositing solutions for film and video artists, game developers, and design visualization professionals; Media and Entertainment Collection that offers end-to-end creative tools for entertainment creation; and 3ds Max software, which provides 3D modeling, animation, and rendering solutions. It sells its products and services through a network of resellers and distributors. Autodesk, Inc. was incorporated in 1982 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo":"Dr. Andrew  Anagnost Ph.D.","headquarters":"San Francisco, CA","employees":14300,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.autodesk.com","price":244.5,"changePercent":-2.60516,"marketCap":51625013248,"peRatio":46.749523,"forwardPE":17.335754,"psRatio":7.1641703,"pbRatio":17.022905,"evToEbitda":27.139,"dividendYield":0,"beta":1.322,"high52Week":329.09,"low52Week":214.1,"avgVolume":2148611},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":7206.000128,"grossProfit":6653.000192,"operatingIncome":1524.8,"netIncome":1124.0,"ebitda":1906.0,"totalAssets":14412.000256,"totalDebt":2734.000128,"cashAndEquivalents":2596.999936,"sharesOutstanding":211.145251,"eps":5.23,"dividendsPerShare":0,"capex":360.3000064,"operatingCashFlow":2452.0}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Technology","summary":"Autodesk, Inc. is well positioned to capture market share in Software - Application.","priceTarget":293.4,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"ADP":{"info":{"ticker":"ADP","name":"Automatic Data Processing, Inc.","sector":"Technology","industry":"Software - Application","description":"Automatic Data Processing, Inc. provides cloud-based human capital management (HCM) solutions worldwide. It operates in two segments, Employer Services and Professional Employer Organization (PEO). The Employer Services segment offers strategic, cloud-based platforms, and human resources (HR) outsourcing solutions. This segment's offerings include RUN Powered by ADP, a software platform for small business payroll, HR, and compliance; ADP Workforce Now, a HCM solution used across mid-sized and large businesses to manage employees; and ADP Lyric HCM, a solution for HR management, payroll, workforce management, talent, and data analytics. The PEO Services segment provides HR and employment administration outsourcing solutions under ADP TotalSource name to businesses through a co-employment model. The segment also provides guidance, user-friendly technology, comprehensive employee benefits, and a risk management, safety, and workers' compensation program. The company was founded in 1949 and is headquartered in Roseland, New Jersey.","ceo":"Ms. Maria  Black","headquarters":"Roseland, NJ","employees":67000,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.adp.com","price":212.995,"changePercent":-0.511468,"marketCap":85141397504,"peRatio":19.887487,"forwardPE":17.526571,"psRatio":3.9416585,"pbRatio":13.437323,"evToEbitda":13.614,"dividendYield":3.19,"beta":0.841,"high52Week":329.93,"low52Week":188.16,"avgVolume":3741173},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":21600.39936,"grossProfit":10475.49952,"operatingIncome":5071.9199232,"netIncome":4345.6,"ebitda":6339.899904,"totalAssets":43200.79872,"totalDebt":4398.000128,"cashAndEquivalents":3228.400128,"sharesOutstanding":399.734282,"eps":10.71,"dividendsPerShare":6.8,"capex":1080.019968,"operatingCashFlow":5452.400128}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Technology","summary":"Automatic Data Processing, Inc. is well positioned to capture market share in Software - Application.","priceTarget":255.594,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"AXON":{"info":{"ticker":"AXON","name":"Axon Enterprise, Inc.","sector":"Industrials","industry":"Aerospace & Defense","description":"Axon Enterprise, Inc. provides public safety technology solutions in the United States and internationally. The company operates in two segments, Software and Services, and Connected Devices. The Software and Services segment develops, manufactures, and sells cloud-based software-as-a-service solutions to capture, store, manage, share, and analyze video and other digital evidence. This segment also offers Axon Evidence, Draft One, Axon Records, Axon Standards, Axon Fusus, Axon Assistant, and others. The Connected Devices segment engages in the development, manufacture, and sale of integrated hardware solutions, such as conducted energy devices under the TASER brand, body cameras, fixed and in-car cameras, drone and counter-drone technologies, accessories, extended warranties, and related hardware products, as well as virtual reality training hardware. The company serves first responders across international, federal, state, and local governments, international governmental entities, commercial enterprises, and consumers through direct sales, distribution partners, and third-party resellers. The company was formerly known as TASER International, Inc. and changed its name to Axon Enterprise, Inc. in April 2017. Axon Enterprise, Inc. was incorporated in 1993 and is headquartered in Scottsdale, Arizona.","ceo":"Mr. Patrick W. Smith","headquarters":"Scottsdale, AZ","employees":5100,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.axon.com","price":403.54,"changePercent":-5.46979,"marketCap":32526163968,"peRatio":164.04065,"forwardPE":38.16573,"psRatio":10.902937,"pbRatio":9.98219,"evToEbitda":326.942,"dividendYield":0,"beta":1