 online retailers, corporate travel management, and financial institutions who leverage its travel technology and tap into its diverse supply to augment their offerings and market Expedia Group rates and availabilities to its travelers. The trivago segment sends referrals to online travel companies and travel service providers from hotel metasearch websites. In addition, it provides brand advertising through online and offline channels, loyalty programs, mobile apps, and search engine marketing, as well as metasearch, social media, direct and personalized traveler communications on its websites, and through direct e-mail communication with its travelers. The company was formerly known as Expedia, Inc. and changed its name to Expedia Group, Inc. in March 2018. Expedia Group, Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Seattle, Washington.","ceo":"Mr. Barry  Diller","headquarters":"Seattle, WA","employees":16000,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.expediagroup.com","price":229.98,"changePercent":-9.0233,"marketCap":27602677760,"peRatio":20.298323,"forwardPE":9.999791,"psRatio":1.8194369,"pbRatio":47.9125,"evToEbitda":10.693,"dividendYield":0.77,"beta":1.3,"high52Week":303.8,"low52Week":156.05,"avgVolume":2464878},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":15171.00032,"grossProfit":13694.999552,"operatingIncome":2077.5999488,"netIncome":1488.0,"ebitda":2596.999936,"totalAssets":30342.00064,"totalDebt":4705.999872,"cashAndEquivalents":5793.999872,"sharesOutstanding":114.498625,"eps":11.33,"dividendsPerShare":1.76,"capex":758.550016,"operatingCashFlow":4858.999808}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Consumer Cyclical","summary":"Expedia Group, Inc. is well positioned to capture market share in Travel Services.","priceTarget":275.976,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]