d running on QIAGEN instruments and technologies; human ID/forensics assay consumables comprising short tandem repeat assays for human ID, and assays for food contamination; PCR instruments, including digital PCR and qPCR solutions; and developed and configured enzymes and PCR solutions. It offers NGS gene panels, library prep kits and components, and whole genome amplification; DNA methylation analysis; QIAGEN consumables and instruments; bioinformatics solutions; and sequence-based assays forensic genetic genealog services. it provides software-as-a-service. It serves molecular diagnostics and life sciences sectors. The company was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Venlo, the Netherlands.","ceo":"Mr. Thierry L. Bernard","headquarters":"Venlo, N/A","employees":5526,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.qiagen.com","price":33.04,"changePercent":-1.40256,"marketCap":6808710144,"peRatio":16.857143,"forwardPE":12.466749,"psRatio":3.2439992,"pbRatio":2.045314,"evToEbitda":10.786,"dividendYield":0.8,"beta":0.642,"high52Week":57.82,"low52Week":32.92,"avgVolume":1968850},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":2098.862976,"grossProfit":1385.164032,"operatingIncome":579.6448256,"netIncome":402.164992,"ebitda":724.556032,"totalAssets":4197.725952,"totalDebt":1646.557056,"cashAndEquivalents":646.289024,"sharesOutstanding":206.074753,"eps":1.96,"dividendsPerShare":0.26,"capex":104.94314880000002,"operatingCashFlow":615.214976}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Healthcare","summary":"Qiagen N.V. is well positioned to capture market share in Diagnostics & Research.","priceTarget":39.648,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"VMED":{"info":{"ticker":"VMED","name":"VMED","sector":"Technology","industry":"Other","description":"","ceo":"N/A","headquarters":"N/A, N/A","employees