raph, The Sunday Telegraph, Herald Sun, Sunday Herald Sun, The Courier Mail, The Sunday Mail, The Advertiser, Sunday Mail, The Sun, The Sun on Sunday, The Times, The Sunday Times, and New York Post, as well as digital mastheads and other websites. In addition, the company publishes general fiction, nonfiction, children's, and religious books; and operates Storyful, a social media content agency, as well as sports radio network and news channels. Further, it offers property and property-related advertising and services on its websites and mobile applications; digital real estate services; and financial services. The company has operations in the United States, Canada, Europe, Australasia, and internationally. News Corporation was incorporated in 2012 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo":"Mr. Robert J. Thomson","headquarters":"New York, NY","employees":22300,"founded":0,"website":"https://newscorp.com","price":27.02,"changePercent":-0.0739662,"marketCap":14786685952,"peRatio":34.20253,"forwardPE":22.200312,"psRatio":1.6803052,"pbRatio":1.7137059,"evToEbitda":13.122,"dividendYield":0.74,"beta":0.902,"high52Week":31.61,"low52Week":22.2,"avgVolume":4407998},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":8800.0,"grossProfit":5015.000064,"operatingIncome":995.9999488,"netIncome":447.0,"ebitda":1244.999936,"totalAssets":17600.0,"totalDebt":2841.999872,"cashAndEquivalents":2171.000064,"sharesOutstanding":364.758219,"eps":0.79,"dividendsPerShare":0.2,"capex":440.0,"operatingCashFlow":997.0}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Communication Services","summary":"News Corporation is well positioned to capture market share in Entertainment.","priceTarget":32.424,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"FSLR":{"info":{"ticker":"FSLR","name":"First Solar, Inc.","sector":"Techn