uty and wellness products for young women aged 25 to 30; and restaurants and event venues, as well as women's apparel subscription rental service under the Nuuly brand. Further, the company designs, develops, and markets young women's contemporary casual apparel, intimates, activewear, and shoes under the Free People and FP Movement brands; and apparel collections under the Urban Outfitters brand. It serves its customers directly through retail stores, websites, mobile applications, catalogs and customer contact centers, franchisee-owned stores, and department and specialty stores, as well as social media and third-party digital platforms. Urban Outfitters, Inc. was founded in 1970 and is based in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.","ceo":"Mr. Richard A. Hayne","headquarters":"Philadelphia, PA","employees":11780,"founded":0,"website":"https://www.urbn.com","price":71.5,"changePercent":1.50482,"marketCap":6412043776,"peRatio":14.130435,"forwardPE":11.050151,"psRatio":1.0400085,"pbRatio":2.2780857,"evToEbitda":8.982,"dividendYield":0,"beta":1.226,"high52Week":84.35,"low52Week":54.44,"avgVolume":1553106},"financials":[{"period":"FY2023","periodType":"annual","revenue":6165.376,"grossProfit":2219.741952,"operatingIncome":592.3215872000001,"netIncome":464.919008,"ebitda":740.401984,"totalAssets":12330.752,"totalDebt":1225.565952,"cashAndEquivalents":695.929984,"sharesOutstanding":85.60128,"eps":5.06,"dividendsPerShare":0,"capex":308.2688,"operatingCashFlow":575.190016}],"earnings":[],"analysts":[],"theses":[{"type":"bull","title":"Growth in Consumer Cyclical","summary":"Urban Outfitters, Inc. is well positioned to capture market share in Apparel Retail.","priceTarget":85.8,"keyDrivers":["Market expansion","Product innovation"],"risks":["Competition","Macroeconomic factors"],"catalysts":["Earnings release","New product launch"],"conviction":"high"}]},"WCRX":{"info":{"ticker":"WCRX","name":"WCRX","sector":"Technology","industry":"Other","description":"","ceo":"N/A","headquarters"